{% comment %}
The summary cell of one advisory in the index table: its CVE and title as the
link, then its id and the states a reader needs to see without opening it.

Shared by the row that spans product rows and the row of a notice naming no
products, so the two cannot drift. Expects `advisory` and `advisory_url`.

Resolved is the one status worth seeing without reading, so it is a badge and
the rest stay muted text. The CVSS badge beside it still says how bad the issue
was, which is a different question from whether it is still open. Withdrawn is
a badge for the opposite reason: a retracted advisory that reads as current is
worse than one that is missing.
{% endcomment %}
{% load humanize %}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
    <a class="text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-text no-underline hover:underline underline-offset-4"
       data-button
       href="{{ advisory_url }}">
        {% if advisory.cve_ids %}
            <span class="font-mono text-text-secondary">{{ advisory.cve_ids|join:", " }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {{ advisory.title }}
    </a>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 [flex-wrap:wrap] text-xs text-text-muted">
        <span class="font-mono">{{ advisory.id }}</span>
        {% if advisory.is_gated %}
            <c-branded.badge brand title="Restricted — shown because you have access to the affected products">
            <i class="fas fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>Restricted
            </c-branded.badge>
        {% endif %}
        {% if advisory.is_withdrawn %}<c-branded.badge tone="medium">Withdrawn</c-branded.badge>{% endif %}
        {% if advisory.status == 'resolved' %}
            <c-branded.badge tone="success">
            <i class="{{ advisory.status_icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ advisory.status_label }}
            </c-branded.badge>
        {% elif advisory.status_label and advisory.affected_rows %}
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><i class="{{ advisory.status_icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ advisory.status_label }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if advisory.withheld_product_count %}
        <p class="text-xs italic text-text-muted my-0">
            {{ advisory.withheld_product_count|intcomma }} further product{{ advisory.withheld_product_count|pluralize }} not shown
        </p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
